{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-800ff8fa-97bb-4f04-af86-7a1f716b0126","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89eb96d044275142","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-o1xgnpoh/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Configure pgvector as the Remote Vector_io Provider for Gen AI Studio Playground RAG\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the vector database integration inside Gen AI Studio: when the gen-ai BFF creates an OGXServer instance for a playground with RAG enabled, it configures OGX's remote pgvector vector_io provider (activated via the ENABLE_PGVECTOR environment guard), reusing the existing remote vector store implementation. The vector database runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX server. OGX's application storage backend is a separate, independent configuration and remains on its existing default — this change does not touch it, and there is no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration concern.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation for playgrounds so that, when RAG is enabled, the vector_io provider is set to the remote pgvector provider instead of relying on the inline provider bundled in the distribution image.\n- Consume the PostgreSQL connection details for the provider from an injectable source (Kubernetes Secret / connection string), designed so the source is swappable: the self-provisioned per-namespace instance today, the platform-provided shared database planned for a later release, or a user-provided external vector database.\n- Scope the vector store per namespace for multi-tenant isolation.\n- Reuse and adapt the existing remote vector store provider implementation rather than writing a new provider.\n- Leave the OGX application storage backend (kv/sql) configuration unchanged from its current default.\n- Keep the configuration additive and revertible: restoring the prior provider configuration returns the playground to its previous behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A playground created with RAG enabled gets an OGXServer instance whose vector_io provider is the remote pgvector provider, and the vector database it talks to runs as a separate process from the OGX server.\n- The provider registers successfully and a basic vector insert/query round-trip works through the remote pgvector provider from the playground.\n- The OGX application storage backend configuration emitted by the BFF is unchanged from its current default.\n- Vector stores are scoped per namespace: a playground in one namespace cannot read or write vector data of a playground in another namespace.\n- The connection source is injectable: pointing the provider at a different connection string (an external database or a shared platform database) requires a configuration change only, no code change.\n- Reverting the configuration change restores the previous vector_io provider behavior.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability): this epic delivers the provider wiring those workflows run on.\n- HLR-4 (default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX/Llama Stack instance): delivered by configuring the remote provider.\n- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box availability): partially covered — the provider wiring half; the database provisioning half is delivered by the selected provisioning implementation.\n- HLR-5 (multi-tenant scoping): per-namespace provider scoping delivered here and verified end-to-end during validation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89438,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95f83f4e9296bd43","agent_id":"a9613ec76490a22b1","session_id":"90eb4e85-7690-4532-889d-850d91d0a9f8","uuid":"3acfc32a-02b8-4136-8260-858722e78056","timestamp":"2026-10