{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-800ff8fa-97bb-4f04-af86-7a1f716b0126","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8749b58398abffde","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-o1xgnpoh/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Operator-Based PostgreSQL/pgvector Provisioning for Gen AI Studio (Operator Path)\n\n## Description\n\nImplemented if the go/no-go decision selects the operator path: the RHOAI-controlled operator layer (delivered by the dashboard operator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164) provisions and manages the PostgreSQL instance with pgvector for Gen AI Studio playgrounds, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern. For each namespace where a playground with RAG is enabled, the operator reconciles the database Deployment, Service, storage, and credentials, and the playground configuration consumes the connection string. No custom container image is built or onboarded: the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image ships pgvector out of the box and is already referenced for disconnected installs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in the RHOAI-controlled operator: reconcile a database Deployment, Service, PersistentVolumeClaim, and credentials Secret per namespace where a playground with RAG is enabled.\n- Reference the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) via the existing related-image environment variable so disconnected installs resolve the reference; no custom image build and no build-pipeline onboarding.\n- Model resource requests/limits on the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing as the starting point.\n- Scope provisioning per namespace for multi-tenant isolation.\n- Expose the connection details as a Kubernetes Secret that the playground's OGXServer vector_io provider configuration consumes.\n- Handle lifecycle: reconciliation back to desired state and cleanup of database resources when the playground is deleted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Enabling a playground with RAG in a namespace results in a ready PostgreSQL-with-pgvector instance with no manual user setup.\n- Database credentials are managed via Kubernetes Secrets, and the connection details are consumable by the OGXServer vector_io provider configuration in that namespace.\n- Deleting the playground cleans up the provisioned database resources.\n- The database runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX server instances in the namespace.\n- No custom container image is built; the image reference resolves through the existing related-image environment variable used for disconnected installs.\n- Resource requests/limits are set from the model-registry-operator reference sizing and recorded in the implementation.\n- Vector data is isolated per namespace.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- This path exists only if the operator layer from the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) is delivered in time for the target release; that timing is externally controlled by the separate in-progress strategy.\n- Planning note (epic size): this epic sits at the upper end of the one-sprint guideline if the modularized operator surface requires more than database deployment templating. Kept as one logical change: a split would separate the resource templates from the reconciliation loop that owns them. Re-split trigger: re-split into (a) CR/spec extension with resource templates and (b) reconciliation and lifecycle management if the operator-layer integration exceeds the estimated surface.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning): delivered by this path.\n- HLR-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance): separate database Deployment.\n- HLR-5 (multi-tenant scoping): per-namespace provisioning.\n- HLR-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments): reference-based resource sizing.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89438,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95f83f4e9296bd43","agent_id":"a9613ec76490a22b1","session_id":"90eb4e85-7690-4532-889d-850d91d0a9f8","uuid":"9131d2bd-2387-46c6-86b6-d62675e263c4","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:39:50.118Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
