ints) are all corroborated by the cited files (`ogx-distribution.md`, `model-registry-operator.md`, `odh-dashboard.md`), so `architecture_claims: +1` with citations is correctly calibrated on all four Implementation epics — no \"no architecture claims\" miss.\n71\t- Plausible differentiations: BRANCH-A's `external_dependency: -1` (hard RHAISTRAT-7164 cross-strategy dependency) vs. BRANCH-B's `+1` (exists to avoid that dependency), and E003's `pattern_precedent/existing_foundation: 0` (new harness) are consistent with the strategy content. Arithmetic/thresholds not checked per instructions (pipeline-computed).\n72\t\n73\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n74\t\n75\t- Every epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated ACs: E002 is a replacement-style configuration change and carries the revert AC (\"Reverting the configuration change restores the previous vector_io provider behavior\") plus the injectable-connection-source AC. No konflux or docs-authoring epics exist, so their mandated ACs do not apply.\n76\t- No misfiled external-precondition ACs: the RHAISTRAT-7164 timing risk is correctly recorded in Risks/Notes (E001, BRANCH-A) and the summary Health Warnings as a schedule risk, never as an AC. E003's baseline AC conditions the epic's own deliverable (measurements captured before inline removal) and its sequencing risk is in Risks/Notes.\n77\t- No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — all cross-references use full RHAISTRAT keys or prose.\n78\t\n79\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n80\t\n81\t- All in-scope strategy acceptance criteria are accounted for: out-of-the-box availability (E002 + branch), playground RAG no-regression (E002/E003), separate-process decoupling (E002/branch/E003), per-namespace scoping (E002/branch/E003), lightweight footprint (branch sizing + E003 measurement). Success criteria covered: no functional regression (E003), no manual setup (branch ACs), RHAISTRAT-7474 unblocked (E003 closing, recorded in Tiered Deliv