{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7ef54ce09209d31","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8004: Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio\n11\t\n12\t## Decomposition Inputs and Fidelity Notes\n13\t\n14\t- The strategy's full body (Affected Components table, Impacted Teams table, HLR table with priorities, Dependencies table, NFRs) is stored as a Jira attachment (`RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`) that is not present in this workspace (attachment fetch is disabled here). The decomposition is derived from the Jira description (summary, problem statement, acceptance criteria, open questions) plus the Staff Engineer Input, which takes precedence over the AI-generated technical approach. HLRs below are derived from the strategy's Acceptance Criteria and prioritized from the strategy frontmatter priority (Blocker → P0). Recorded as a health warning below.\n15\t- The Staff Engineer Input is non-empty and authoritative; every divergence from the AI-generated strategy text is logged in the Staff Engineer Input Overrides section.\n16\t\n17\t## Epic List\n18\t\n19\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n20\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n21\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 | Go/no-go decision: PostgreSQL provisioning approach for the default vector store | Investigation | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | Configure pgvector as the remote vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground RAG | Implementation | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Validate the pgvector default vector store: benchmark, functional no-regression, resource sizing | Implementation | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 | Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (operator path) | Implementation (branch A) | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playground (fallback path) | Implementation (branch B) | dashboard-crimson-scrum | P0 |\n26\t\n27\tMain-plan epics: E001–E003. Branch epics are conditional alternatives attached to the gating investigation; exactly one of them is built, per the go/no-go outcome.\n28\t\n29\t## Dependency DAG\n30\t\n31\tMain plan (roots at top; `A --> B` means A must complete before B starts):\n32\t\n33\t```mermaid\n34\tgraph TD\n35\t    E001[\"E001 Go/no-go investigation\"]\n36\t    E002[\"E002 pgvector provider wiring\"]\n37\t    E003[\"E003 Validation and benchmark\"]\n38\t    E001 --> E003\n39\t    E002 --> E003\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\tConditional branches (excluded from the main-plan critical path):\n43\t\n44\t```mermaid\n45\tgraph TD\n46\t    E001[\"E001 Go/no-go investigation\"]\n47\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E004 Operator-based provisioning\"]\n48\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E004 BFF-managed provisioning\"]\n49\t    E001 --> BA\n50\t    E001 --> BB\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\t## DAG Justification\n54\t\n55\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n56\t|------|------|-----------|\n57\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (investigation gates downstream, true gate `rewrite`) | The validation scope depends on which provisioning path the go/no-go selects; validation cannot be scoped or run before the decision. |\n58\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (consumer ordering) | Validation exercises the provider wiring E002 delivers; the validation report cannot be produced before the wiring exists. |\n59\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E004, E001 → BRANCH-B-E004 | Rule 3 (true gate `remove`) | Each branch epic exists only under its outcome; the go/no-go decision selects which one is built. Bounded outcomes (2) → conditional branches rather than phased decomposition. |\n60\t| No edge E001 → E002 | Step 5.5 tiered delivery / Rule 17 analog | The provider wiring is identical under every provisioning outcome — Tier 1 independent work that delivers partial value and de-risks while the gate is pending. |\n61\t| No edge E002 ↔ BRANCH-A/B-E004 | Rule 13 (configuration-reference exception) | The PostgreSQL connection string the provider config consumes is a configuration reference filled in at execution time, not a build-against artifact. Expressed as the injectable-connection-source acceptance criterion on E002, never as a DAG edge. |\n62\t| No edge BRANCH-*-E004 → E003 | Branch rule (main-plan epics never depend on branch epics) | E003 depends on the investigation (E001) whose outcome selects the branch; in execution, validation follows the selected branch's implementation. |\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n65\t\n66\tHLRs are derived from the strategy's Acceptance Criteria (the HLR table lives in the unavailable strategy attachment). All are P0 per the strategy's Blocker priority — there are no P1/P2 HLRs, so no priority-split analysis applies and no lower-priority HLR is folded into a higher-priority epic.\n67\t\n68\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic(s) | Notes |\n69\t|-----|----------|-------------|---------|-------|\n70\t| HLR-1 | P0 | A default vector store is available out-of-the-box without manual provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure | RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 (provider half); RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 or RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 (provisioning half — exactly one, per go/no-go outcome) | Provisioning approach selected by E001 |\n71\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability | RHAISTRAT-8004-E002, RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | |\n72\t| HLR-3 | P0 | Auto Rag functions with the default vector store with no loss of current capability | — (removed from scope) | Removed per Staff Engineer Input: Auto Rag compatibility with pgvector is RHAISTRAT-7824's scope (RHOAI 3.6). Deliberately not covered here; see Health Warnings. |\n73\t| HLR-4 | P0 | The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider) | RHAISTRAT-8004-E002; RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 / RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004; verified in RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | |\n74\t| HLR-5 | P0 | The default vector store is scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation) | RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 (provider scoping); RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 / RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004; verified in RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Per-namespace confirmed: the per-instance concern was Auto Rag's, now decoupled |\n75\t| HLR-6 | P0 | The default vector store is lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments without significant overhead | RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 / RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004; measured and adjusted in RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Sizing modeled on the model-registry-operator reference |\n76\t\n77\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides\n78\t\n79\tLogged for traceability (Staff Engineer Input takes precedence over the AI-generated technical approach):\n80\t\n81\t1. **Auto Rag removed from scope** (affected components, impacted teams, acceptance criteria, validation requirements) — RHAISTRAT-7824 owns Auto Rag/pgvector compatibility targeting RHOAI 3.6. HLR-3 above reflects this.\n82\t2. **Corrected the PostgreSQL premise**: OGX does not auto-provision PostgreSQL — it defaults to SQLite for application storage, and the gen-ai BFF hardcodes SQLite when creating OGXServer instances. Introducing PostgreSQL for vectors is new work, not an extension of existing infrastructure.\n83\t3. **No custom image build, no Konflux onboarding**: `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` already includes pgvector, the model-registry-operator already auto-provisions it, and the related-image environment variable is already in the rhods-operator CSV for disconnected installs. The strategy's 1–2 sprint image-onboarding estimate is eliminated — no `repo-onboarding`, `konflux-onboarding`, or `license-validation` epics are generated.\n84\t4. **Vector storage and application storage are independent configurations**: only the pgvector vector_io provider is configured; the SQLite application-storage backend is untouched, and there is no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration concern.\n85\t5. **Performance thresholds, corpus-size ranges, and index-type selection removed as open questions**: dev-experimentation scope — order-of-magnitude benchmark against the inline Milvus baseline, flat scan at default scale, no SLA thresholds.\n86\t6. **Platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC arrives no earlier than RHOAI 3.6**: for the current release Gen AI Studio must provision its own instance — hence the go/no-go between operator-based and BFF-managed self-provisioning, with bring-your-own PostgreSQL as the last-resort fallback.\n87\t\n88\t## Component Mapping Notes\n89\t\n90\t- gen-ai BFF work (odh-dashboard repo, `packages/gen-ai`) → canonical component `Gen AI Studio` (the product capability the BFF serves).\n91\t- Operator-layer provisioning (branch A — the RHOAI-controlled operator delivered by the dashboard operator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164) → canonical component `AI Core Dashboard`.\n92\t- OGX distribution and ogx-k8s-operator are **passive** here (no code changes; keep working): the remote pgvector vector_io provider already exists in the OGX distribution, corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/ogx-distribution.md` (PGVector listed as an optional vector DB backend; remote-only provider set after inline-provider stripping; providers activated via environment-variable guards). Their continued function is validated as acceptance criteria on E002/E003 rather than separate epics — the same owning team validates.\n93\t- Rule 22 (infrastructure not in platform inventory) was evaluated for the PostgreSQL image: existence and working precedent are corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/model-registry-operator.md` (controller-created `{registry-name}-postgres` Deployments/Services/Secrets), so no separate existence-validation Investigation is generated; functional validation is folded into E003.\n94\t\n95\t## Health Warnings\n96\t\n97\t- **Missing strategy attachment (fidelity)**: the full strategy body (HLR table, Affected Components, Impacted Teams, Dependencies, NFRs) is a Jira attachment not present in this workspace. HLRs were derived from the acceptance criteria and prioritized from the strategy's Blocker priority. If the attachment becomes available, re-check HLR wording, any NFRs (disconnected-install behavior, sizing constraints), and any Documentation Support requirement against this epic set.\n98\t- **External timing risk (schedule risk, not an AC)**: the primary provisioning path depends on the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164, in progress), whose delivery timing is outside this strategy's control and cannot be compressed. Recorded as a risk on E001 and branch A — it is an input to the go/no-go decision, never an acceptance condition.\n99\t- **Planning note (epic size)**: the operator-based provisioning epic (branch A) sits at the upper end of the one-sprint guideline if the modularized operator surface requires more than database deployment templating. Kept as one logical change: a split would separate the resource templates from the reconciliation loop that owns them. **Re-split trigger**: re-split branch A into (a) CR/spec extension with resource templates and (b) reconciliation and lifecycle management if the operator-layer integration exceeds the estimated surface.\n100\t- **Scope boundary — Auto Rag**: the strategy title and one acceptance criterion name Auto Rag, but Staff Engineer Input removes it to RHAISTRAT-7824 (RHOAI 3.6). Watch for double coverage between this strategy's validation and RHAISTRAT-7824's scope at review and planning time.\n101\t- **Open question disposition**: the migration-path question (default vector store → production-grade vector database) does not change which epics exist — the pgvector provider sits behind OGX's standard remote vector_io interface, so moving to an external vector database is reconfiguration. Captured as the injectable-connection-source acceptance criterion on E002 rather than a separate epic. The scoping-model question is resolved as per-namespace for Gen AI Studio (the per-instance concern was Auto Rag's, now decoupled).\n102\t\n103\t## Tiered Delivery\n104\t\n105\tThe external dependency (RHAISTRAT-7164 operator-layer timing) has uncertain timing, and partial value is deliverable without it:\n106\t\n107\t- **Tier 1 (independent, start immediately)**: E002 — the remote pgvector provider wiring is identical under every provisioning outcome; it delivers the vector_io integration and de-risks the reuse assumption while the go/no-go is pending.\n108\t- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 — the provisioning implementation selected by the go/no-go decision, which is itself contingent on the RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery forecast. The bring-your-own-PostgreSQL option (users configure the OGXServer CR spec with their own connection details, aligned with OGX 1.0 breaking changes) is the recorded last-resort fallback if neither self-provisioning path is viable.\n109\t- **Closing**: E003 validates the assembled capability (wiring + selected provisioning path) and closes the strategy's no-regression acceptance criteria; RHAISTRAT-7474 (inline provider removal) is unblocked once validation passes.\n110\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a218fb04822f2eb9","agent_id":"ab262741f7e8a609b","session_id":"90eb4e85-7690-4532-889d-850d91d0a9f8","uuid":"16dd5815-df6c-4252-8985-1cb9fb153947","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:46:01.903Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7ef54ce09209d31","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004"}
