{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-848e25aa6f6fa877","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Validate the pgvector default vector store: benchmark, functional no-regression,\n4\t  resource sizing'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the go/no-go decision activates the bring-your-own-PostgreSQL\n17\t    fallback (neither self-provisioning path is viable), the validation scope is rewritten\n18\t    to cover the user-configured external database path instead of platform self-provisioning.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 5\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Validate the pgvector Default Vector Store: Benchmark, Functional No-Regression, and Resource Sizing\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tValidates that the default vector store preserves the out-of-the-box Gen AI Studio playground RAG experience once the inline provider is removed from the OGX distribution. Captures the inline Milvus baseline and verifies that pgvector performs in the same order of magnitude on representative playground RAG workloads — strict latency SLAs are explicitly not required, since the default instance is scoped for development experimentation, not production usage. Confirms functional no-regression, per-namespace isolation, and a lightweight resource footprint, and adjusts the PostgreSQL resource requests/limits if the benchmark indicates.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Capture the inline Milvus provider baseline on representative playground RAG workloads (small document sets, flat scan — no vector index required at default scale).\n45\t- Benchmark the pgvector default vector store on the same workloads and compare order of magnitude.\n46\t- Run Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows end-to-end against the assembled default vector store (provider wiring plus the selected provisioning path): document ingestion, retrieval, and generation.\n47\t- Verify per-namespace isolation of vector data.\n48\t- Record the resource footprint of the provisioned PostgreSQL instance against the model-registry-operator's resource requests/limits as the reference starting point, and adjust sizing if the benchmark results indicate.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- The inline Milvus baseline measurements are captured and recorded before the inline provider is removed from the distribution.\n53\t- A benchmark report exists showing pgvector within the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline on the representative workloads, with the workload definitions attached.\n54\t- Playground RAG workflows (ingestion, retrieval, generation) pass end-to-end with the default vector store, with no loss of capability relative to the current inline-provider experience.\n55\t- Per-namespace isolation is verified: cross-namespace vector data access fails.\n56\t- The provisioned database's resource requests/limits are recorded, match or are deliberately adjusted from the model-registry reference sizing, and fit a resource-constrained environment envelope.\n57\t\n58\t## Risks / Notes\n59\t\n60\t- The baseline must be captured on a build that still carries the inline provider, i.e. before the inline-provider removal tracked in RHAISTRAT-7474 lands. Sequencing with that strategy is a coordination risk on this epic's schedule, not a dependency of its deliverable.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability): verified here end-to-end.\n65\t- HLR-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance): verified as part of the end-to-end run.\n66\t- HLR-5 (multi-tenant scoping): isolation verified here.\n67\t- HLR-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments): footprint measured and sizing adjusted here.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a218fb04822f2eb9","agent_id":"ab262741f7e8a609b","session_id":"90eb4e85-7690-4532-889d-850d91d0a9f8","uuid":"3fbecec2-628c-417d-9e67-b0585ece41dd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:46:05.671Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-848e25aa6f6fa877","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004"}
